00:32:37,683 --> 00:32:38,933
The pressure will subside.

737
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:41,516
We are to believe it and expect it.

738
00:32:42,233 --> 00:32:43,150
And here's the thing.

739
00:32:43,983 --> 00:32:46,150
If not in this life, just like David.

740
00:32:46,683 --> 00:32:49,150
We can expect, and we see Jesus.

741
00:32:49,783 --> 00:32:50,833
Everything will be new.

742
00:32:53,383 --> 00:32:55,150
Therefore, we can rejoice.

743
00:32:56,533 --> 00:32:59,650
So this morning, I wonder, Are you choosing

744
00:33:00,483 --> 00:33:01,783
to rejoice?

745
00:33:03,583 --> 00:33:06,599
Do you walk around and every time something doesn't go your way, you become

746
00:33:06,599 --> 00:33:09,599
sour and bitter and resentful and you forget

747
00:33:09,599 --> 00:33:12,716
all the things that God promises, you forget all the things God said and

748
00:33:12,733 --> 00:33:15,966
you just, you sit there in your feelings and and you

749
00:33:15,966 --> 00:33:17,700
think, okay, this is just what I am right now.

750
00:33:17,766 --> 00:33:18,299
No, no, no.

751
00:33:19,883 --> 00:33:21,366
Understand joy comes in the morning.

752
00:33:23,283 --> 00:33:24,250
His anger is real.

753
00:33:25,533 --> 00:33:26,883
His chastisement is real.

754
00:33:27,583 --> 00:33:29,583
Our sins effect on our life is real.

755
00:33:31,533 --> 00:33:32,833
But joy comes in the morning.

756
00:33:34,033 --> 00:33:36,966
What David is trying to tell us is, rejoice in hope.

757
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:39,299
Just like Paul wrote.

758
00:33:39,366 --> 00:33:40,916
So what are you rejoicing in?

759
00:33:41,049 --> 00:33:41,700
Are you rejoicing?

760
00:33:42,233 --> 00:33:43,933
What has Ben Eis closed all over this place?
